From: Zander Brown <zbrown@gnome.org>
Date: Wed, 13 Nov 2024 15:06:07 +0000
Subject: shared-closures: handy <closure> functions

We were getting increasingly close to having identical closure
implemenations in multiple types, instead have this header to share them

(cherry picked from commit b2b60558c9626f4596eb0c4fec768aa39e96c873)

Origin: upstream, future 48 alpha
---
 src/kgx-shared-closures.h | 38 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/meson.build           |  1 +
 2 files changed, 39 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/kgx-shared-closures.h

diff --git a/src/kgx-shared-closures.h b/src/kgx-shared-closures.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c0d1807
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/kgx-shared-closures.h
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
